  "story": {
    "title": "Historians say King Verica persuaded Rome to invade Britain. But could Verica actually have been a queen?",
    "summary": "An archaeologist has put forward a controversial theory that Verica, the British ruler traditionally said to have urged Rome to invade, may have been a woman rather than a king. If true, it would change how we tell the story of the Claudian landing in Kent in AD43.",
